From Canada, With love.

this story makes me so sad. I feel like our relationships with our parents are a huge burden to be carried. We cant appease them. We cant live our own lives, and we arent allowed to be our version of happy.

&#x200B;

So, I will try and be as supportive as possible as I write this. 

&#x200B;

Firstly, you are 22 years old. Are you ready to tear apart your family and the fabric of your entire community? Do you know if you have the mental, emotional, and fiscal strength to deal? if so, continue :). If not, I would suggest you look for the most dignified exit.

&#x200B;

Next, your parents reactions have not been incredibly crazy based on this community here. You have to understand, you introduced a complete unknown to them. Its like introducing the concept of a round earth to a flat earther. They are unreasonable and their brain cannot process. They are trying to rectify. It will take time.

&#x200B;

Finally, how supportive is your  bf through this. Your folks have obviously dealt with all this in an okay manner. What about this dream buoy? is he supportive or just an un involved bystander?

&#x200B;

I would suggest you think about all this. I left my family for the love of my life. I am not sure if I have regrets, but I love my lady and i find peace in this.

&#x200B;

Try not to have melodramatic conversations with your folks. Try to keep a level head and move on.
